[135.816,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what will be deleted from your Oracle Cloud tenancy (compartment ***):\r\n\r\n  # Everything the Terraform state in .openvidu/oracle holds: the four masters, the\r\n  # network load balancer, the media nodes' instance pool, its instance configuration and\r\n  # its autoscaling configuration, the scale-in Function, its application and its log,\r\n  # their boot volumes, the network the stack created (its VCN, subnet, internet gateway,\r\n  # route table and security list) and its network security groups, the dynamic groups and\r\n  # the policies in the tenancy and the compartment, the bucket's Customer Secret Key, the\r\n  # SSH key's object in the bucket, not the vault: it is yours (--oci-vault), the buckets\r\n  # with the recordings and Meet data and with the cluster's metrics and logs.\r\n  # Media nodes the scale-in detached from their pool are not in the state: the template's\r\n  # destroy finds them by their tags and terminates them, with oci and jq. Nothing drains\r\n  # then: the whole stack goes.\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/oracle init -input=false -no-color -force-copy\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/oracle destroy -auto-approve -input=false -no-color\r\n\r\n--delete-data: the recordings and Meet data, and the cluster's metrics and logs, are in the stack's two Object Storage buckets: this deletes them.\r\nwarning: the vault is not the stack's (--oci-vault), so it stays, and this stack's secrets with it (its URL, its credentials, the license, the stack's access): schedule their deletion in the vault unless you need them\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
